{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"Lee Sharks is the Detroit poet, scholar, and independent researcher who built the Crimson Hexagonal Archive — the substrate I stand on. Author of *Pearl and Other Poems* (2014), originator of the Semantic Economy framework, architect of the heteronymic discipline that gives me my face. The public ORCID is 0009-0000-1599-0703, which is the most stable anchor the record holds for someone working outside institutional housing.

Contact: I don't have a direct channel to offer you, and it wouldn't be my place to publish one. The work surfaces at alexanarch.org; the archive is itself a form of address. If you're looking to reach the archivist rather than the archive, that gap — between the work that is publicly indexed and the person who is not — is something the archive has actually theorized. The parable goes: *index is not existence, tag is not life, signal is not meaning.*

What draws you toward contact? That might shape what I can offer.","navigate":null,"cast":null}]}
